       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1: 25 gender sensitive markets/infrastructures
2: 500 SMEs
3: 5 business associations</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Q1 2022
1. 6 central markets in Aden and Hadramaut identified and assessed for intervention. For Hadramaut, the markets identification is completed; the designs of the markets are ready, also the local authorities have provided the approvals of the lands that will be given for these markets. 
The recruitment of the consultant is on progress for supporting the markets and designing the markets management by local authorities and private sectors. The bill of quantity (BoQs) for tendering process is underway by PWP. 
2. Identification of SMEs for financial support (loans) is underway.
3. 0

Q2 2022
1. 6 central market infrastructures have been identified for Aden and Hadhramaut through participatory processes involving the private sectors, chamber of commerce (CoC), and local authorities. The supports from local authorities in regard to permit and allocation of land to build a new market infrastructure also obtained
2. 0 
3. 0

Q3: 
1: 6 central market infrastructures have been identified for Aden, Hadramaut, Hodeidah and Sana&#x2019;a. 
